 "said": {
  "text": "the Android console app needs Pilot and axHub tabs like the web console's App tabs plugin. Option A: every tab runs inside the app — Build Pilot (pilot.amberxai.com) and axHub (axhub.amberxai.com, Apps page + approvals) in locked-down in-app web views; nothing ever opens the phone's browser. Fable (the Compose AppShell gains the shared page slots the web shell has). Broken into small builds (sub prompts) so it can be worked on a little at a time; each sub prompt stands alone and leaves the app building.",
  "verbatim": false,
  "at": "2026-10-20T00:00:00Z",
  "source": "",
  "by": "backfill",
  "addenda": []
 },
 "brief": "# Dev Console as an Android app: wrapper, one codebase (Brett, Nov 7)\n\nBrett chose the wrapper over a native rewrite: the existing web console runs inside an Android app shell, same way AmberX loads its web plugins. One codebase; every console change shows on the phone at once.\n\nReuse: orchestrator build `console-android-app-tabs` (19 steps, pending) — get its brief (`node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs brief console-android-app-tabs`) and use what fits; ignore the archived native rewrite `console-android-native-tabs`. Reuse AmberX's Android shell/bridge pieces (apps/amberx-droid) rather than writing new ones.\n\n1. Android app shell loading the console (console.amberxai.com), with sign-in kept, back button/navigation, pull-to-refresh, offline screen.\n2. Native bridges where needed: push notifications (build start/finish/fail/land alerts), mic for voice, background wake, file share/download (APKs), deep links that open a console screen.\n3. Console UI stays asset-driven; phone layouts come from the existing three-layouts/phone assets, no hard-coded styling.\n4. APK built in CI next to amberx-debug.apk; listed under Apps in the console/axHub for install.\n5. UI Review with three options (--choices) for the shell chrome. Tests. Add to Shipped features.\n\nProgress: append `<time> START|DONE <step>` to PROGRESS.md here at each step; don't stop between steps. Commit, don't push.",
